#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:3
#: 89c22b70b84445baa75163bbb790f106
msgid "Usability & UX Guidelines"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:5
#: 5b77510a808048cd94ba2f16779af769
msgid ""
"Unnecessary complexity and bad UI often scare users away from good software. "
"To avoid this terrible fate, please always take usability and good user "
"experience into account when contributing to Qubes OS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:7
#: 7de01af02e9249f89bd5aece916a11d0
msgid ""
"If you plan to contribute to GUI tools, please read these guidelines. "
"Additional information can also be found in our `visual style guide <https://"
"www.qubes-os.org/doc/visual-style-guide/>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:10
#: e3ce584e15754c129a69aff6e7d271ac
msgid "Ease of Use"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:12
#: 888dfa98841144c1b681be9898c6aa8a
msgid ""
"In open source software, a good user interface should not only enable users "
"to achieve their goals, but also allow them to remain in control of the "
"process. The UI should neither overwhelm the users with the amount of "
"information presented nor hide important context from them. In the words "
"falsely attributed to Albert Einstein: our goal is to make things as simple "
"as possible, but not simpler. Make things simple, but removing important "
"elements in the name of simplicity or getting rid of valuable functionality "
"for simplicity's sake is making them too simple."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:14
#: 32502d1ae37e453b88979d671a1f7c52
msgid "Make sure that the UI you design adheres to the following principles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:17
#: 796061748baa4d5ea884138b3a4d51ce
msgid "Do not waste the user's time"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:19
#: c8696c5ade8649a18190598bef90c33e
msgid "the program should not *require* extensive configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:20
#: 3a99db8e48e84184a3bc0a547d3f735f
msgid ""
"**example**: you don't need to set the policy directory used by "
"the :program:`Qubes Policy Editor` - the program lists available policy "
"files for you"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:21
#: 81919d45bb1042e592319fe856a0cd5d
msgid ""
"the most typical and most recommended workflows should require the least "
"user time and attention"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:22
#: 07bf6b005d2a438382b40a5b0e0ed73f
msgid ""
"**example**: :guilabel:`Create New Qube` opens at the typical use-case (a "
"new app qube) with options such as \"template\" and \"networking\" set to "
"system defaults; the user only has to enter qube name and click ``Create``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:23
#: a9d9aeb33d4842f892174e016f55b82b
msgid ""
"the defaults should be sensible - they should work for most use cases and "
"not require changes in most situations, if at all possible"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:24
#: 32857bd43e504c58aa40e89d196bdaf7
msgid "**example**: default settings for newly created qubes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:25
#: cde2bfdedcce424fa31631e13ee38568
msgid ""
"minimize repetitiveness: if possible, avoid multiple clicks or multiple "
"steps for operations that can be implemented with less clicks/steps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:26
#: 00b04cc432e144388764e223d75cfebb
msgid ""
"**example**: in the ``Devices widget``, if a device is already attached to a "
"qube, you have an option to ``Detach`` the device, but also to ``Detach and "
"Attach`` to another qube - the user doesn't have to do two actions, but only "
"one"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:29
#: c94c8f65b445464baacf076abaf7d30f
msgid "Make the UI resilient to errors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:31
#: c04336fbac5044dc830115837094185f
msgid ""
"users should not be able to break the program (or the entire system) or "
"enter an unrecoverable state"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:32
#: 51982d3fc3f14dc3a8b1098493922746
msgid ""
"users should not be able to compromise the integrity and security of their "
"system accidentally"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:33
#: 09691b5b49c143beb8cc7b7e9f5eeccc
msgid "as far as possible, there should be a possibility to undo actions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:34
#: 3e0f94f4791c4bdd852a7f59d84009a4
msgid ""
"if some actions cannot be undone (for example deleting a qube), they should "
"be impossible to perform accidentally (in case of Qubes OS, you have to type "
"the qube name to delete it, even using GUI tools)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:35
#: 98b646721ff244269da0d0daa64e2df7
msgid "the defaults should be reasonably secure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:36
#: 53e877774dc5488a9668a3f603bb26d5
msgid ""
"avoid leaving users stranded - if there is an error message, there should "
"also be guidance on how to recover or (preferably) an actionable solution"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:39
#: 8378bb54850641538252935bcffa18ff
msgid "Reduce cognitive load"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:41
#: 5075d003162c43e38158d69362f63459
msgid "show only the relevant information"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:42
#: 90baaba5f98e4c8184e17d6dd1b0326e
msgid ""
"**example**: domains widget does not show qubes that are not running and not "
"consuming resources"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:43
#: bf01d1824e294ce797ecc13748ec71db
msgid "use simple and understandable language"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:44
#: 9c446ea4628944a7a4d850c3c9777e92
msgid ""
"when in doubt, like the author of this document, always use the simpler word "
"and don't write like it's a master's thesis in English literature"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:45
#: f9579efcd95b49a6b4583474897f3b49
msgid "make it easy to discover and understand features and available options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:46
#: bf16154aa7aa45138ea532bfae2397cf
msgid ""
"**example**: :guilabel:`Qubes Global Config` aims to show and describe "
"multiple configuration settings that otherwise were only available via CLI "
"and knowing about them"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:47
#: 0b3a363a48b34f9694060558a541307d
msgid ""
"do not expect the user to remember: remind them of past actions and choices"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:48
#: c097ec74c2b54578a9469fc9987fc034
msgid ""
"**example**: during the update process, show which qubes are being updated "
"right now, which are still queued for updated and which are done updating"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:49
#: 1002cd70eae74e66bfefcaf7ffb52711
msgid ""
"the defaults should make sense for most use cases and not require the user "
"to verify them thoroughly"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:50
#: 5a19ac369542449d8c3646f86a5855b1
msgid ""
"**example**: a new qube will use the default template and default networking "
"settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:54
#: caf6550fc746497d8cbb27a5953644e2
msgid "Language"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:56
#: 13fce79123074071ab60b8f72f873bba
msgid ""
"There will always be the need to communicate things to users. In these "
"cases, an interface should aim to make this information easy to understand. "
"The following are simple hints to help achieve this - as with any writing "
"advice, those are guidelines, not laws."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:59
#: f6415109c9684dfaa523a86ee315f551
msgid "Avoid acronyms"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:61
#: 508b5a8c89ca4a1e8ae04617dbe2dfa7
msgid ""
"Acronyms are compact and make good names for command line tools, but until "
"the user learns an acronym’s meaning, it is gibberish. Avoid introducing new "
"acronyms, unless necessary, and provide explanations if the acronym is "
"uncommon. Some acronyms are more familiar than the full name - it is "
"strongly recommended to use USB instead of Universal Serial Bus, for example."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:64
#: 56456cc631764135814526c426ef422f
msgid "Use simple words"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:66
#: b7fc885487484cf78914e5bc29368775
msgid ""
"Use the minimum amount of words needed to be informative. Go with common "
"words that are as widely understood. \"Unneeded\" is better than "
"\"superfluous\", \"correct\" is better than \"rectify\" and \"pointless\" is "
"better than \"nugatory\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:69
#: 28944034add34feb938c8b3752e6417a
msgid "Follow current Qubes OS terminology"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:71
#: f28667e1d43748188e7df6392eac3bd5
msgid ""
"use **disposable [qube]** instead of ``DVM`` or ``Disposable Virtual "
"Machine``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:72
#: caa8358a204d49d183a5ab3c4a61bfb6
msgid "use **networking** or **net qube** instead of ``NetVM``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:73
#: eec7f467022341148bf073fc65f1bf5b
msgid ""
"use **qube** instead of ``virtual machine``, ``container``, ``domain`` or "
"``domU``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:74
#: bd0eee7fdd8842808e8225012a464eca
msgid ""
"use terminology consistent with other user-facing tools, not necessarily "
"with internal programming details"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:77
#: 74e98a9a7a4b42a4b397c05c8ef4e534
msgid "Avoid technical words"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:79
#: 4cf3771b1c564cdaaca3a0ec1ea3a6aa
msgid ""
"Technical words are usually more accurate, but they often *only* make sense "
"to technical users and are confusing and unhelpful to non-technical users. "
"Strive for accuracy and usefulness above strict technical correctness. If at "
"any point you wish to add to a label a \"well, actually\", resist the "
"temptation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:81
#: 5889ca0ca0134a73b149b11de4aaa5ed
msgid ""
"Prefer a common, understandable concept to detailed technical explanations "
"of a particular implementation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:82
#: b1adc0770b9248e39e5523339735ce9c
msgid ""
"Use ``disk space`` instead of ``root.img``, since while not quite accurate, "
"it makes contextual sense"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:83
#: 526d4a230e0e43ce9d366edeb417a378
msgid ""
"Use ``saving`` instead of ``savefile`` as the former is the action trying to "
"be completed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:84
#: 9d788df6a8704bab85f21a1404e5bb51
msgid ""
"Use ``Qubes`` instead of ``qrexec-daemon`` as it gives better context on "
"what is happening"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:87
#: 43f1f325cb1a40a9b5f2d61bcc02ef78
msgid "Avoid redundancy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:89
#: aca5d00523f040d1975b3073ee4dd3d9
msgid "do not over-use words like ``qube`` or ``domain`` in long lists"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:90
#: 41c3a361920d4e2f9d81ad077264446b
msgid ""
"it is preferable to create common categories/headers than to repeat a single "
"category multiple times"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:92
#: 4f97f794db69441f8910efd1530b46af
msgid "Qubes 3.2 system menu with redundant 'domain' prefix to every qube name"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:95
#: 61d57eddc5a944c6b9c2b190dc40eecb
msgid ""
"System menu in Qubes 3.2 used to make both of those mistakes: redundant "
"'domain' prefix and no category headers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:98
#: 69909d5102b94444b52cb87441b091c4
msgid "Usability and Accessibility"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:100
#: c25c4ee75a5b46b6ad02e41ab26b2935
msgid ""
"Usability and accessibility are always tied together. When designing "
"interfaces for Qubes OS, follow general good UI practices, striving for "
"understandability, clarity of interactions, avoid surprising the user, avoid "
"- as far as possible - actions that cannot be undone and strive to make it "
"easy to do the correct/secure action and difficult to do the insecure action."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:102
#: 8f2d6c5b356940ddb2e5cb015fe8d4f6
msgid ""
"Use the checklist below to verify fundamental accessibility and usability "
"principles:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:104
#: 6f3bb823baa64e6495c922ebde455165
msgid "**visual readability**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:105
#: 50d67bab3b8d4ebdb0e4277016e83262
msgid ""
"there is sufficient contrast between text and background (use `WCAG level AA "
"guidelines <https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG21/>`__ as minimum when in doubt)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:106
#: 14021dadcb5c498fbe2cc8e3d8eeef2a
msgid "UI remains readable in dark mode and in light mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:107
#: 6abd8de8e939464cb991344f9836ea2c
msgid "**color independence**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:108
#: 0dbe62e8b7f84e0fa7e26966a4cb843d
msgid ""
"important information is never communicated solely through color: labels, "
"text, shapes etc. accompany all color-coded information"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:109
#: 9a09c2928d654b3fb98021b3311b314f
msgid "**text scaling support**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:110
#: e020a5db7fba4db4808f17b885971245
msgid ""
"the program works for large font sizes (including what you might consider "
"absurdly large)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:111
#: bcfce217371d40ef9cb4df943b016bab
msgid "**keyboard/mouse accessibility**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:112
#: e946f94849fe46f783812a082ecedf96
msgid ""
"all actions can be reached and performed when using only the keyboard and "
"only the mouse without exorbitant leaps of logic or reading the documentation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:113
#: 20146b4a756144a58d792e56db455925
msgid "tab-order for controls is logical"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:114
#: 5fcb75e13eed492ba0aef276988d8924
msgid "**focus visibility**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:115
#: 736cf37130ef49699a03c5829a24afe9
msgid ""
"it is always visible which element has focus, when using keyboard navigation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:116
#: f83dc87cd4c248bc87c62ba3eac4f6a7
msgid "focus is not irrevocably lost on some operations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:117
#: b7b434b9cd1b4d4aab81b6cdc494c4e2
msgid "**clarity and communication**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:118
#: c91be179eda7444b8b0ccb353a6b2988
msgid ""
"language used in the GUI is clear, understandable and simple; avoid complex "
"sentences and overly complex vocabulary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:119
#: 3669b77eed4e42f786c901c629691098
msgid ""
"error messages are specific and visible; if possible, errors are accompanied "
"by information about how to recover from them (ideally, this would be done "
"automatically, but of course this is not always possible)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:120
#: c2b4b672c27f464f8010112e44b5b578
msgid ""
"validation is always clearly communicated: the user can easily understand "
"why certain inputs are incorrect"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:121
#: 467eca7f84874c668f33b3418e9518b9
msgid "error and validation feedback does not rely on timing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:124
#: 29e5c234ed324d7489057c447562fdea
msgid "Consistency and UI Elements"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:126
#: 387b45a2778f4514bea3be48d0e23399
msgid ""
"Concepts, names, icons, interaction patters and styling should be consistent "
"across different tools. When in doubt, pattern the behavior of your "
"application on other Qubes OS tools."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:128
#: ec35a135e95a49948cf7f06730d9d9bf
msgid "Particular GUI patterns used in Qubes OS are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:131
#: b414ae5d385e47c5b547ddf47470cbba
msgid "Qube names"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:133
#: 3de3d34688b44471895c05e4cbc6b8cf
msgid ""
"Qube name should be whenever possible accompanied by the appropriate qube "
"icon in the correct color."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:136
#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:182
#: c3f3b4998e3e4fafbca880a2633f39b4 08ad4229e8e94e638f06f3a07c88f61c
msgid "Examples:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:138
#: de858394f9794dd1a24f377beab1b029
msgid ""
"part of Qubes OS Global Config: two dropdowns used to configure Clock qube "
"and Default net qube. In both dropdowns, the qube names are accompanied by "
"the qube icon to their left"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:141
#: c993c85a76ff48ce950f8975a2e3ad71
msgid ""
"Dropdowns in :guilabel:`Qubes OS Global Config` contain icons. Always use "
"existing dropdown widgets if possible: they generally already provide the "
"icon display."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:144
#: 31fa13c3dd384707980abbc074ae9b5c
msgid ""
"part of Create New Qube Dialog showing selected net qube with its icon to "
"the left of the qube name"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:147
#: 695bae93ba0448faa0351c89f6ebf44d
msgid ""
"In :guilabel:`Create New Qube` Dialog, selected network qube is displayed "
"with its icon and also with the qube color used to color the qube name, to "
"reinforce the qube-label association."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:149
#: 9fef5b92b1d741d79632108e69b5bf23
msgid ""
"list of running qubes from the domains widget; each qube name has the qube "
"icon to the left of it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:152
#: f6b3185c8661449c96477393752268fc
msgid "In the domains widgets, every qube is always accompanied by its icon."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:155
#: 8f6a7f3772b14fea8f6bda8406d11acc
msgid "Action buttons"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:157
#: 80f8eea4ce1f4efe8f32af67c408cab8
msgid ""
"If possible, any button should have a brief and understandable description "
"of the action it will cause if pressed written on the button itself. Avoid "
"generic \"OK\" buttons. Usually only one button should be marked visually as "
"the main \"confirmation\" button. If there are multiple buttons who could "
"serve this role, individual discernment must be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:160
#: c00702998eee4504b680d34bf784ba35
msgid "Use flat buttons."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:162
#: 8ecf7257a92949008fed412dfc3d1f9f
msgid ""
"Use the following CSS classes (with appropriate text size and padding) for "
"confirm and cancel buttons:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:180
#: acbb5a158bc64777a888c4c61c37deb8
msgid ""
"For color definitions, see :ref:`below <developer/general/usability-"
"ux:Colors>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:184
#: cb5348641d1b4ef0af2b96035c18f290
msgid ""
"part of Qubes OS Global Config: three buttons at the bottom of the screen. "
"Blue button with text \"Apply Changes and Close\", and two flat normal "
"buttons with text \"Apply Changes\" and \"Cancel\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:187
#: ed38ca3a72af4450b27edd4333836d9b
msgid ""
"The visually marked button is \"Apply Changes and Close\", because this is "
"assumed to be the typical interaction with the tool."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:189
#: 462d0d2f2fa24493a9e6d67e114b2208
msgid ""
"part of Policy Editor: three buttons at the bottom of the screen. Flat "
"button with text \"Quit\" and two blue buttons with \"Save changes\" and "
"\"Save and exit\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:192
#: f9623b5ba1c1487eb551b3ed55acfec1
msgid ""
"Button text should be brief and clear. Two actions seemed to be typical for "
"the interaction with the tool (saving and exiting and saving without "
"exiting), so both are emphasised."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:196
#: da416d2397e34741bb62355a87594c79
msgid "Icons"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:198
#: a430fd8fe1394875b6cb58d444c520af
msgid ""
"Core of Qubes OS Icon Set is the set of qube-related icons that can be found "
"in the `qubes-artwork <https://github.com/QubesOS/qubes-artwork/tree/main/"
"icons/scalable/apps>`__ repository."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:200
#: a0caa04063c94e4ca636e63349ec5e01
msgid ""
"Those icons represent possible qube classes and colors. For mapping of qube "
"icon to qube type, see the :doc:`/user/reference/glossary`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:202
#: 83962ba5c2df47f49bcea96083559c17
msgid ""
"Most symbolic icons in Qubes GUI are taken from `lucide.dev <https://"
"lucide.dev>`__ (MIT-licensed open source icon set)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:204
#: 9f61416a5361472c8a46e0dc29c764d5
msgid ""
"The following stroke width is generally recommended for the following icon "
"sizes (adjusted when needed for clarity and cohesion):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:206
#: 428e047ca3ac4dcd8bb5509d03977f30
msgid "16px = 1.5px stroke"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/usability-ux.rst:207
#: 9b316b041b774a1ba97ada7566d7b8c4
